You can add a hover effect to your `.btn` class by using the `:hover` pseudo-class. Here's the updated CSS with a hover function:  

```css
.btn {
  padding: 20px;
  cursor: pointer;
  border: none;
  color: #fff;
  border: 2px solid white;
  width: 120px;
  height: 100px;
  margin: 20px;
  text-transform: capitalize;
  transition: all 0.3s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transition effect */
}

.btn:hover {
  background-color: white;
  color: black;
  transform: scale(1.1); /* Slightly enlarges the button on hover */
}
```

This will make the button slightly larger, change the background color to white, and the text color to black when hovered. Let me know if you need further tweaks! 🚀
